WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.094 --> 00:00:01.428
and conventional and long-range

00:00:01.562 --> 00:00:03.630
rockets for U.S. Provided.

00:00:03.764 --> 00:00:04.331
Additional information on the

00:00:04.465 --> 00:00:06.700
security package can be found on

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:07.101
defense.gov.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:08.902
In regards to our announcement

00:00:09.036 --> 00:00:10.604
last night regarding the high

00:00:10.737 --> 00:00:11.338
altitude surveillance balloon,

00:00:11.472 --> 00:00:14.241
I'm not going to have much new

00:00:14.374 --> 00:00:14.942
information to provide other

00:00:15.075 --> 00:00:17.044
than to say the North American

00:00:17.177 --> 00:00:17.778
aerospace defense command

00:00:18.112 --> 00:00:19.546
continues to monitor it closely.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.116
While we won't get into

00:00:22.216 --> 00:00:23.117
specifics in regards to the

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.852
exact location, I can tell you

00:00:24.985 --> 00:00:26.920
that balloon continues to move

00:00:27.054 --> 00:00:28.255
eastward an is currently over

00:00:28.388 --> 00:00:29.389
the center of the continental

00:00:29.523 --> 00:00:30.190
United States.

00:00:30.324 --> 00:00:31.625
Again, we currently assess that

00:00:31.758 --> 00:00:33.427
balloon does not present a

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.595
military or physical threat to

00:00:34.728 --> 00:00:36.597
people on the ground at this

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:38.999
time, and we'll continue to

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.301
monitor and review options.

00:00:41.435 --> 00:00:42.402
Finally, secretary Austin will

00:00:42.536 --> 00:00:44.938
host a bilateral meeting today

00:00:45.072 --> 00:00:46.840
here in the Pentagon with

00:00:46.974 --> 00:00:48.142
Australian deputy prime minister

00:00:48.142 --> 00:00:51.545
and minister of defense Richard

00:00:51.678 --> 00:00:52.513
morals.

00:00:52.646 --> 00:00:54.148
Looks forward to discussing

00:00:54.148 --> 00:00:55.015
bilateral defense cooperation

00:00:55.149 --> 00:00:56.283
and mutual security efforts

00:00:56.416 --> 00:00:58.352
within the indo-pacific and

00:00:58.485 --> 00:00:58.685
beyond.

00:00:58.852 --> 00:01:01.755
A full readout we'll post later

00:01:02.156 --> 00:01:03.490
today to defense.gov.

00:01:03.624 --> 00:01:06.160
We'll move to your questions and

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:06.426
start with ap.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.060
&gt;&gt; Hi, pat.

00:01:07.194 --> 00:01:08.562
Thank you for doing this.

00:01:08.695 --> 00:01:10.164
China has said this is just a

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.598
weather balloon that has veered

00:01:11.732 --> 00:01:12.799
off course.

00:01:12.933 --> 00:01:14.935
Why is the Pentagon convinced

00:01:15.068 --> 00:01:16.270
this is a surveillance balloon

00:01:16.403 --> 00:01:18.172
and then, can you give us a

00:01:18.172 --> 00:01:19.006
little bit more on the status of

00:01:19.139 --> 00:01:20.174
the balloon?

00:01:20.174 --> 00:01:22.576
You said it's in the central --

00:01:22.709 --> 00:01:23.310
central U.S.

00:01:23.443 --> 00:01:24.178
What state?

00:01:24.178 --> 00:01:25.245
Do you have any guidance for

00:01:25.379 --> 00:01:27.181
people as they see this balloon

00:01:27.314 --> 00:01:28.782
or trying to photograph it or

00:01:28.916 --> 00:01:31.418
try to interfere with it?

00:01:31.552 --> 00:01:32.386
&gt;&gt; Thanks, Tara.

00:01:32.519 --> 00:01:34.888
First of all we are aware of the

00:01:35.022 --> 00:01:35.522
prc's statement.

00:01:35.656 --> 00:01:37.691
However, the fact is, we know

00:01:37.824 --> 00:01:40.294
that it's a surveillance

00:01:40.427 --> 00:01:42.196
balloon, and I'm not going to be

00:01:42.196 --> 00:01:43.263
able to be more specific than

00:01:43.397 --> 00:01:43.564
that.

00:01:43.697 --> 00:01:44.932
We know that balloon has

00:01:45.065 --> 00:01:47.334
violated U.S. Air space and

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:49.636
international law which is

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:50.470
unacceptable and we've conveyed

00:01:50.604 --> 00:01:53.540
this directly to the prc at

00:01:53.674 --> 00:01:54.975
multiple levels, and in terms of

00:01:55.108 --> 00:01:56.510
specific locations, I'm not

00:01:56.643 --> 00:01:57.544
going to be able to go into

00:01:57.678 --> 00:01:59.780
specific locations, again, other

00:02:00.214 --> 00:02:02.216
than to say it's moving eastward

00:02:02.216 --> 00:02:03.217
at this time.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.619
&gt;&gt; You had a follow-up?

00:02:05.752 --> 00:02:06.954
&gt;&gt; Follow-up on as people start

00:02:07.087 --> 00:02:09.556
to see the balloon, do you have

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:10.224
any guidance?

00:02:10.224 --> 00:02:11.758
Should they try not to interfere

00:02:11.892 --> 00:02:12.259
or photograph?

00:02:12.392 --> 00:02:14.228
&gt;&gt; So the balloon is currently

00:02:14.228 --> 00:02:15.662
assessed to be at about 60,000

00:02:15.796 --> 00:02:19.366
feet, so again, well above the

00:02:19.499 --> 00:02:21.568
range of civilian air traffic or

00:02:21.702 --> 00:02:24.271
where civilian air traffic would

00:02:24.404 --> 00:02:26.240
normally fly.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:27.874
Certainly aware that there are

00:02:28.242 --> 00:02:29.176
cameras, you know, civilian

00:02:29.309 --> 00:02:30.844
owned commercial cameras that

00:02:30.978 --> 00:02:33.580
could spot this balloon in terms

00:02:33.714 --> 00:02:35.082
of guidance to folks, again,

00:02:35.215 --> 00:02:37.284
this is something that norad is

00:02:37.417 --> 00:02:38.252
closely monitoring.

00:02:38.252 --> 00:02:41.822
We do assess at this time that

00:02:42.256 --> 00:02:45.259
it's not pose a physical threat

00:02:45.392 --> 00:02:46.493
as I mentioned to people on the

00:02:46.627 --> 00:02:50.264
ground.

00:02:50.264 --> 00:02:50.364
Jennifer?

00:02:50.497 --> 00:02:52.266
&gt;&gt; General Ryder, who is

00:02:52.366 --> 00:02:54.368
controlling this balloon right

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:54.635
now?

00:02:54.768 --> 00:02:58.672
&gt;&gt; Again, we know that this is a

00:02:58.805 --> 00:03:00.274
Chinese balloon but beyond that

00:03:00.374 --> 00:03:00.941
I will not have specifics.

00:03:01.074 --> 00:03:03.010
&gt;&gt; You say it's moving east ward

00:03:03.143 --> 00:03:05.012
and over the continent U.S., not

00:03:05.145 --> 00:03:06.546
over Montana anymore.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:07.848
Is the Chinese government

00:03:08.282 --> 00:03:08.682
controlling the movement of the

00:03:08.815 --> 00:03:11.051
balloon or is it just floating

00:03:11.184 --> 00:03:12.286
with air streams?

00:03:12.286 --> 00:03:12.919
&gt;&gt; Thanks, Jennifer.

00:03:13.053 --> 00:03:16.290
I'm not going to go into any

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.491
specific intelligence we may

00:03:17.624 --> 00:03:17.791
have.

00:03:17.924 --> 00:03:19.893
Again, we know this is a Chinese

00:03:20.294 --> 00:03:22.296
balloon and that it has the

00:03:22.296 --> 00:03:24.531
ability to maneuver, but I'll

00:03:24.665 --> 00:03:25.499
leave it at that.

00:03:25.632 --> 00:03:27.634
&gt;&gt; Once it's over a body of

00:03:27.768 --> 00:03:29.803
water, will you shoot it down?

00:03:29.936 --> 00:03:31.972
&gt;&gt; Again, right now we're

00:03:32.306 --> 00:03:32.873
monitoring the situation

00:03:33.006 --> 00:03:34.308
closely, reviewing option, but

00:03:34.441 --> 00:03:35.509
beyond that I'm not going to

00:03:35.642 --> 00:03:36.710
have any additional information.

00:03:36.843 --> 00:03:38.312
We go to Tony.

00:03:38.445 --> 00:03:40.714
&gt;&gt; One quick on the balloon, can

00:03:40.847 --> 00:03:43.350
you confirm the photos that are

00:03:43.483 --> 00:03:44.351
out there that this is not the

00:03:44.484 --> 00:03:47.220
man in the moon and that is the

00:03:47.354 --> 00:03:47.788
actual balloon?

00:03:47.921 --> 00:03:49.089
&gt;&gt; Thanks, Tony.

00:03:49.222 --> 00:03:51.124
Certainly aware of photos being

00:03:51.258 --> 00:03:51.591
posted online.

00:03:51.725 --> 00:03:53.493
I'm not going to get into the

00:03:53.627 --> 00:03:55.862
business of confirming whether

00:03:55.996 --> 00:03:56.897
or not those are, you know,

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:58.332
where those photo comes from.

00:03:58.332 --> 00:03:59.800
Again, I can tell you that U.S.

00:03:59.933 --> 00:04:02.636
Government, norad, is monitoring

00:04:02.769 --> 00:04:03.570
this closely and we will

00:04:03.704 --> 00:04:04.705
continue to review options.

00:04:04.838 --> 00:04:06.606
&gt;&gt; How close was the U.S. To

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.742
ordering -- was the president to

00:04:08.875 --> 00:04:10.344
ordering a shoot down of the

00:04:10.344 --> 00:04:10.510
balloon?

00:04:10.644 --> 00:04:12.913
&gt;&gt; Again, I'm not going to get

00:04:13.046 --> 00:04:14.581
into discussions, internal

00:04:14.715 --> 00:04:15.449
discussions, within the white

00:04:15.582 --> 00:04:16.416
house again.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.385
Right now we assess that there

00:04:18.518 --> 00:04:20.354
is no threat, physical threat or

00:04:20.487 --> 00:04:21.188
military threat, to people on

00:04:21.321 --> 00:04:22.022
the ground.

00:04:22.356 --> 00:04:24.458
We're continuing to monitor, you

00:04:24.591 --> 00:04:25.992
know, and we'll leave it at

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:26.426
that.

00:04:26.426 --> 00:04:29.429
Thank you.

00:04:29.563 --> 00:04:35.736
&gt;&gt; Thanks.

00:04:35.869 --> 00:04:36.570
I have two questions.

00:04:36.703 --> 00:04:39.639
In response to secretary

00:04:39.773 --> 00:04:42.542
Austin's recent remarks that

00:04:42.676 --> 00:04:48.448
more U.S. Has started -- when it

00:04:48.582 --> 00:04:49.116
comes to South Korea, north

00:04:49.249 --> 00:04:52.386
Korea want stronger provocations

00:04:52.452 --> 00:04:53.186
in the near future.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:55.655
What is your comment?

00:04:55.789 --> 00:04:59.025
&gt;&gt; Well, certainly not

00:04:59.159 --> 00:05:01.995
surprising given North Korea's

00:05:02.396 --> 00:05:04.965
track record of making bellicose

00:05:05.098 --> 00:05:05.599
statements again.

00:05:05.732 --> 00:05:08.034
What we're focused on is

00:05:08.402 --> 00:05:09.436
preserving peace, security and

00:05:09.569 --> 00:05:11.505
stability in the indo-pacific

00:05:11.638 --> 00:05:11.838
region.

00:05:11.972 --> 00:05:12.839
Secretary Austin's visit was an

00:05:12.973 --> 00:05:14.040
opportunity to reaffirm our

00:05:14.408 --> 00:05:15.509
strong and close alliance with

00:05:15.642 --> 00:05:16.910
the republic of Korea and so

00:05:17.043 --> 00:05:19.946
that will remain our focus.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.982
Working with South Korea and

00:05:22.416 --> 00:05:25.552
other nations in the region to

00:05:25.685 --> 00:05:28.422
deter aggression and ensure a

00:05:28.455 --> 00:05:29.389
free and open indo-pacific.

00:05:29.523 --> 00:05:32.993
&gt;&gt; South Korea has announced it

00:05:33.126 --> 00:05:38.432
will be past the high powered

00:05:38.498 --> 00:05:45.005
ballistic missile with a nuclear

00:05:45.138 --> 00:05:45.605
warhead.

00:05:45.839 --> 00:05:48.642
A defense against North Korea's

00:05:48.775 --> 00:05:49.709
nuclear warhead, how do you

00:05:49.843 --> 00:05:50.444
greet this?

00:05:50.577 --> 00:05:51.211
&gt;&gt; I'm sorry.

00:05:51.878 --> 00:05:54.114
I missed the first part of your

00:05:54.448 --> 00:05:54.481
question.

00:05:54.614 --> 00:05:56.583
&gt;&gt; South Korea has announced

00:05:56.716 --> 00:06:00.987
the -- that it will be a test a

00:06:01.121 --> 00:06:03.323
high-powered monster ballistic

00:06:03.457 --> 00:06:07.761
missile with a war -- nuclear

00:06:07.894 --> 00:06:08.094
warhead.

00:06:08.462 --> 00:06:08.762
This is the --

00:06:08.895 --> 00:06:09.296
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:06:09.429 --> 00:06:12.466
I don't have anything on that.

00:06:12.566 --> 00:06:14.000
I would refer you to the

00:06:14.134 --> 00:06:14.835
government of South Korea.

00:06:14.968 --> 00:06:16.470
I'll come back over here.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:18.004
&gt;&gt; Thank you very much.

00:06:18.138 --> 00:06:22.142
Two questions on the Chinese

00:06:22.476 --> 00:06:22.976
government.

00:06:23.109 --> 00:06:25.078
So -- this balloon flew over

00:06:25.212 --> 00:06:26.980
Japanese air space before

00:06:27.113 --> 00:06:28.515
reaching the U.S. Continental

00:06:28.648 --> 00:06:30.717
U.S., can you confirm that?

00:06:30.851 --> 00:06:32.486
&gt;&gt; I've seen those press

00:06:32.586 --> 00:06:32.786
reports.

00:06:32.919 --> 00:06:34.621
Again, as we acknowledged in our

00:06:34.754 --> 00:06:37.691
statement that we posted last

00:06:37.824 --> 00:06:39.659
night, we have seen this type of

00:06:39.793 --> 00:06:42.028
balloon activity elsewhere

00:06:42.162 --> 00:06:43.730
before, but again, I'm not going

00:06:43.864 --> 00:06:45.599
to get into intelligence, and

00:06:45.732 --> 00:06:46.900
I'm not going to have any

00:06:47.033 --> 00:06:48.502
further information to provide.

00:06:48.502 --> 00:06:51.137
&gt;&gt; Secondly, how will this

00:06:51.271 --> 00:06:53.440
incident affect the secretary's

00:06:53.573 --> 00:06:55.342
future engagement with Chinese

00:06:55.475 --> 00:06:56.710
counterpart to maintain the open

00:06:56.843 --> 00:06:57.777
lines of communication?

00:06:57.911 --> 00:06:59.379
&gt;&gt; I think we've been very clear

00:06:59.513 --> 00:07:01.348
that we're always open to

00:07:01.481 --> 00:07:03.984
maintaining an open line of

00:07:04.117 --> 00:07:07.354
communication with the prc and

00:07:07.487 --> 00:07:08.855
in that regard nothing has

00:07:08.989 --> 00:07:09.389
changed.

00:07:09.523 --> 00:07:09.723
Nothing.

00:07:09.856 --> 00:07:11.291
To Phil and then come over.

00:07:11.424 --> 00:07:14.761
&gt;&gt; The position of the balloon

00:07:14.895 --> 00:07:15.161
classified?

00:07:15.295 --> 00:07:16.530
&gt;&gt; Phil, right now what we're

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.098
not going to do is get to an

00:07:18.532 --> 00:07:19.666
hour by hour location of the

00:07:19.799 --> 00:07:20.534
balloon.

00:07:20.534 --> 00:07:22.035
Again, we're monitoring it

00:07:22.168 --> 00:07:22.536
closely.

00:07:22.536 --> 00:07:24.538
As I mentioned right now, it's

00:07:24.571 --> 00:07:26.540
over the center of the

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:27.007
continental United States.

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:28.108
That's about as specific as I'm

00:07:28.542 --> 00:07:28.975
going to get.

00:07:29.109 --> 00:07:31.611
&gt;&gt; I understand it might be

00:07:31.745 --> 00:07:32.612
inconvenient but does the public

00:07:32.746 --> 00:07:34.848
not have a right to know.

00:07:34.981 --> 00:07:37.717
&gt;&gt; The public has the ability to

00:07:37.851 --> 00:07:38.552
look up in the sky and see where

00:07:38.585 --> 00:07:39.786
the balloon is.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:40.186
Thank you.

00:07:40.554 --> 00:07:43.657
&gt;&gt; General, you said balloon is

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:44.090
maneuverable.

00:07:44.224 --> 00:07:46.560
So does that mean that it's not

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:46.893
drifting?

00:07:47.027 --> 00:07:50.564
&gt;&gt; So the balloon is

00:07:50.564 --> 00:07:50.730
maneuverable.

00:07:50.864 --> 00:07:52.799
Clearly it's violated U.S. Air

00:07:52.933 --> 00:07:54.568
space and again, we've

00:07:54.668 --> 00:07:57.237
communicated that fact to the

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:57.537
prc.

00:07:57.671 --> 00:07:59.039
&gt;&gt; If possible, can you tell us

00:07:59.172 --> 00:08:01.308
if the balloon, when it entered

00:08:01.441 --> 00:08:03.510
the U.S. Air space, has it

00:08:03.643 --> 00:08:06.580
changed its course in any way?

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:09.983
&gt;&gt; The balloon has changed its

00:08:10.116 --> 00:08:11.184
course, which is why we're

00:08:11.318 --> 00:08:11.785
monitoring it.

00:08:11.918 --> 00:08:13.653
That's as specific as I can get.

00:08:13.787 --> 00:08:16.590
Thank you.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:17.390
To Matt.

00:08:17.524 --> 00:08:21.194
&gt;&gt; You said at this point the

00:08:21.328 --> 00:08:22.596
balloon doesn't pose risk to

00:08:22.596 --> 00:08:22.762
citizens.

00:08:22.896 --> 00:08:24.598
How is it that the U.S. Can

00:08:24.598 --> 00:08:25.699
assess that, given that balloon

00:08:25.832 --> 00:08:27.867
is at such an altitude without

00:08:28.001 --> 00:08:29.035
actually getting eyes on it up

00:08:29.169 --> 00:08:30.170
close and assessing the

00:08:30.604 --> 00:08:32.272
equipment that's on board?

00:08:32.606 --> 00:08:35.475
Secondly, are there any

00:08:35.609 --> 00:08:36.610
alternatives considered to

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:37.677
shooting it down or options to

00:08:37.811 --> 00:08:39.179
take the balloon out of the sky

00:08:39.312 --> 00:08:41.247
intact to get a better look at

00:08:41.381 --> 00:08:41.715
that equipment?

00:08:41.848 --> 00:08:42.082
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:08:42.215 --> 00:08:45.986
So again, this is a surveillance

00:08:46.119 --> 00:08:47.554
balloon, you know, operating at

00:08:47.687 --> 00:08:51.558
about 60,000 feet.

00:08:51.691 --> 00:08:52.826
Clearly, you know, we did a he

00:08:52.959 --> 00:08:54.861
very close assessment in terms

00:08:54.995 --> 00:08:58.632
of what it's doing and, as I

00:08:58.665 --> 00:08:59.265
mentioned, military commanders

00:08:59.399 --> 00:09:02.636
have assessed that there is no

00:09:02.636 --> 00:09:03.603
physical or military threat to

00:09:03.737 --> 00:09:06.272
people on the ground.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.642
And so in that regard, we'll

00:09:08.642 --> 00:09:10.644
continue to monitor it.

00:09:10.644 --> 00:09:11.878
In terms of way ahead, we will

00:09:12.012 --> 00:09:14.047
continue to review options, but

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:15.482
I'm not going to have anything

00:09:15.615 --> 00:09:17.417
further to provide on that.

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:20.654
Thank you.

00:09:20.654 --> 00:09:20.787
Matt?

00:09:20.787 --> 00:09:22.656
&gt;&gt; Thank you, pat.

00:09:22.789 --> 00:09:24.190
You said this is violating our

00:09:24.324 --> 00:09:24.891
air space, so why not take it

00:09:25.025 --> 00:09:29.129
down in?

00:09:29.262 --> 00:09:30.664
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:09:30.664 --> 00:09:32.799
As we assess options and

00:09:32.932 --> 00:09:34.668
